# Free API hunter — put free-tier provider keys here (git-ignored, never committed).
# Copy this file to store/free-api-keys.conf and fill in any key you have.
# The hunter tests each key against the live provider and auto-wires the first
# working one into the app (server/.env + GitHub Actions secret).
#
# Get a free key in ~1 minute:
#   Groq        https://console.groq.com       -> GROQ_API_KEY
#   OpenRouter  https://openrouter.ai          -> OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#   Cerebras    https://cloud.cerebras.ai      -> CEREBRAS_API_KEY
#   Gemini      https://aistudio.google.com    -> GEMINI_API_KEY
#   GitHub      https://github.com/marketplace/models -> GITHUB_TOKEN (pat with models:read)
#   DeepSeek    https://platform.deepseek.com  -> DEEPSEEK_API_KEY (paid, cheap)
#
#GROQ_API_KEY=
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
#CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
#GEMINI_API_KEY=
#GITHUB_TOKEN=
#DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Optional: a GitHub PAT that can WRITE repo secrets (Settings -> Developer
# settings -> Fine-grained tokens, repo = whatsapp-automation, permissions:
# Actions = Read and write, or a classic token with the 'repo' scope). When
# set, the free API hunter uses it to push USER_LLM_* / webhook secrets to the
# repo so the live worker gets them on deploy. Falls back to the git credential
# helper token otherwise (which usually can't write secrets).
#GITHUB_SECRETS_TOKEN=
